  "notes": "From English \"pack.\" Has two main meanings in Japanese: packaging/containers and skincare face masks.\n\nSENSE 1 — PACKAGING:\n- {真空|しんくう}パック: vacuum pack\n- {牛乳|ぎゅうにゅう}パック: milk carton\n- {小分|こわ}けパック: individual portion pack\n- パックする: to package/seal\n\nSENSE 2 — FACE MASK:\n- フェイスパック: face pack/mask\n- シートパック: sheet mask\n- パックをする: to apply a face mask\n\nOTHER COMPOUNDS:\n- パック{旅行|りょこう}: package tour\n- {六|ろく}パック: six-pack (of drinks or abs)\n\nNote: {牛乳|ぎゅうにゅう}パック refers to the paper carton, not a plastic container. In Japan, rinsed milk cartons are commonly recycled at supermarkets.",
